  "reporting": {
    "retain": "All declared cases and policy failures remain in raw results. No resampling based on outcome. A completed run may return no feasible incumbent.",
    "feasibility": "Only a complete schedule passing independently implemented constraint and fee checks counts as feasible. A heuristic failure is not a proof of model infeasibility.",
    "primaryComparator": "Cheapest complete feasible result among all five baselines in each case; additionally report strongSearch-only paired comparison.",
    "denominators": "Paired case counts, missing-baseline/optimizer counts, zero denominators and failure rates. Report absolute KRW, total-fee percentage and modeled incremental-fee percentage; sum-weighted denominator. Preserve negative savings and zero ties.",
    "feeBase": "Modeled incremental cost subtracts a fixed fee base computed as of the day before horizon; not evidence of actual paid/sunk accounting cost.",
    "timing": "Per policy wall time plus engine runtime where available; model optimality and time-limit status separately. Do not infer same runtime budget.",
    "sensitivity": "Reuse the same eight base scenarios across variants by design. Report own-tariff costs and reprice all optimized schedules under default reference tariff; neither alternative contracts nor misspecified proxy are asserted official. Compare default-ref objective costs and changed schedule fraction. Single-objective tie-breaking must be disclosed; if unverified, mark ablation as tie-sensitive rather than contribution proof.",
